# Exa

> Exa is a real-time knowledge index and retrieval platform built for AI agents. Exa builds and maintains its own index and search models, and continuously indexes the live web alongside structured data about companies, people, financial markets, code, documents, and other sources. Developers use Exa’s APIs to search, retrieve, and research public and private data.

**Start for free:** New accounts receive $10 in free credits every month, plus a one-time $10 bonus for completing onboarding. No payment method is required, and the free tier includes access to all API endpoints.

For AI agents and automation, start with the agent-native interfaces below. For complete technical documentation, use the Exa documentation index.

## Authentication

The Exa API takes an API key, which a user creates in the dashboard. The hosted MCP server also takes OAuth. /search and /contents also accept x402 pay-per-request payments.

- [Authentication guide for agents](https://exa.ai/auth.md)
- [API keys](https://dashboard.exa.ai/api-keys)

## MCP Server

Connect Exa search, code search, content retrieval, and research tools to Claude, Cursor, Codex, VS Code, and other MCP-compatible clients.

The hosted MCP server can be tried without an API key at limited usage levels.

- [Exa MCP](https://exa.ai/mcp)
- [MCP documentation](https://exa.ai/docs/get-started/exa-mcp.md)
- [Hosted MCP server](https://mcp.exa.ai/mcp)
- [MCP server repository](https://github.com/exa-labs/exa-mcp-server)

## Agent Skills

Install reusable skills that teach coding agents how to search, retrieve content, research companies, generate leads, and build applications with Exa.

- [Agent Skills](https://exa.ai/docs/get-started/agent-skills/overview.md)
- [Agent Skills repository](https://github.com/exa-labs/agent-skills)

